  "fields": {
    "title": "HTML",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "HTML, short for HyperText Markup Language, is the standard markup language for documents designed to be displayed in a web browser. HTML describes the structure of a web page semantically. It can be supported by other languages such as ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "3TBGoqMl1snjRBxLIzrc6Z",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "CSS",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ", which defines the look and layout of content, or JavaScript, which affects the behaviour and content of web pages. Web browsers receive HTML documents from a web server or from local storage and render these documents into multimedia web pages.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "6gTIVxCdxgJzzJvvqTmhZz",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[1]",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The first page of a website is typically named ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "index.html ",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "and needs to include the following tags: ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "html, head",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " and",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " body. ",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "You don't need to have separate documents for styling (style.css) and scripting (script.js), even if it keeps your files better organised, you can also put the style and script tag inside your html file. ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Background",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "In 1980, physicist Tim Berners-Lee, a contractor at CERN, proposed and prototyped ENQUIRE, a system for CERN researchers to use and share documents. In 1989, Berners-Lee wrote a memo proposing an Internet-based hypertext system. Berners-Lee specified HTML and wrote the browser and server software in late 1990.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "6gTIVxCdxgJzzJvvqTmhZz",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[1]",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " HTML is based on SGML (Standard Generalised Markup Language), a markup language that was used at CERN and had already become established there. The first HTML version at that time contained just 21 elements (for comparison: the current HTML 5 version contains 121 elements). One of the most characteristic HTML elements is probably the anchor element, also called ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "70YjtGRCs4BUACjaqQzlDY",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "hyperlink",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ", which makes it possible to link to any resource within the web.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Syntax",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "HTML consists of a series of elements, which you use to enclose, or wrap, different parts of the content to make it appear a certain way, or act a certain way. You can see all HTML Elements, that are explained in this glossary by filtering the entries for HTML (but of course there are a lot more html elements out there to explore).",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "embedded-asset-block",
          "data": {
            "target": {
              "sys": {
                "id": "6Qof1RZiWxVCts5pYA94Vo",
                "type": "Link",
                "linkType": "Asset"
              }
            }
          },
          "content": []
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The main parts of a HTML element are these:",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "ordered-list",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "list-item",
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "paragraph",
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "The opening tag:",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": " ",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ],
                      "data": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "This consists of the name of the element (in this case, p), wrapped in opening and closing angle brackets",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": ". ",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ],
                      "data": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "This states where the element begins or starts to take effect — in this case where the paragraph begins.",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "list-item",
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "paragraph",
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "The closing tag:",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": " ",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ],
                      "data": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "This is the same as the opening tag, except that it includes a ",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "forward slash ",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ],
                      "data": {}
                    },
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "before the element name. This states where the element ends — in this case where the paragraph ends. Failing to add a closing tag is one of the standard beginner errors and can lead to strange results.",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "list-item",
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "paragraph",
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "The content: This is the content of the element, which in this case, is just text.",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "list-item",
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "paragraph",
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "The element: The opening tag, the closing tag, and the content together comprise the element.",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Elements can also have attributes that look like the following:",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "embedded-asset-block",
          "data": {
            "target": {
              "sys": {
                "id": "77cXBW0rpGmtiPmau2rask",
                "type": "Link",
                "linkType": "Asset"
              }
            }
          },
          "content": []
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Attributes contain extra information about the element that you don't want to appear in the actual content. Here, ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "class",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " is the attribute, while ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "editor-note",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " is the attribute value. The ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "class",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " attribute allows you to give the element a non-unique identifier that can be used to target it (and any other elements with the same ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "class",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " value) with style information and other things.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "An attribute should always have the following:",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "ordered-list",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "list-item",
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "paragraph",
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "A space between it and the element name (or the previous attribute, if the element already has one or more attributes).",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "list-item",
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "paragraph",
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "The attribute name followed by an equal sign.",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "list-item",
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "paragraph",
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "nodeType": "text",
                      "value": "The attribute value wrapped by opening and closing quotation marks.",
                      "marks": [],
                      "data": {}
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
